; The file routines, one a module (a segment of its own each). Their INT 21h
; calls were seen in a -dos trace of a start up to the map (open 78 times at
; S2C8E:0047, close at S2B85:0015, reads at S2B8F, S2C01 and S2C45, the
; allocation at S2CBE:0037); what the arguments mean is read from the code.
name S2C8E:0006 file_open
comment S2C8E:0006 file_open(mode, far name): INT 21h AH=3Dh, AX = handle or 0. Mode 1 takes another path (presumably create; not checked).
name S2B85:0002 file_close
comment S2B85:0002 file_close(handle): INT 21h AH=3Eh.
name S2B8F:000C file_size
comment S2B8F:000C file_size(far name): opens, reads eight bytes; a packed file's signature is tested, else the size comes from a seek to the end. Presumably DX:AX = the unpacked size (the packed path was not read to its end).
name S2C01:0006 lib_read
comment S2C01:0006 Presumably reads one named entry of a library file: opens [BP+0A], reads a dword and seeks there, then reads 0Ch-byte records while the name at [BP+0E] is not empty (read from the code's start only).
name S2C45:0002 file_load
comment S2C45:0002 file_load(far buffer or 0/FFFFFFFF, far name, ...): opens, reads eight bytes, unpacks a packed file, else reads it whole; allocates when no buffer is given (read from the code; the unpacking itself was not read).
name S2CBE:000E mem_alloc
comment S2CBE:000E mem_alloc(dword size): INT 21h AH=48h for size/16+1 paragraphs; the segment is entered in the table at DATA:0469 (count at DATA:0467) and returned in DX, AX = 0.

; Shows a text of GAME.TXT by its number in one side's status line: its
; callers pass 3Eh, 52h and 64h where the screen shows the quit question,
; the F1 line and the thinking time (runs with screenshots).
name S10AF:000F show_message
comment S10AF:000F show_message(text number, side)

